      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/22687"
      cmd         : "#!/bin/bash
  {
  datadir=$(/bin/grep -h '^datadir' /etc/mysql/mysql.conf.d/*.cnf /etc/mysql/my.cnf /etc/my.cnf 2>/dev/null | /bin/awk -F= '{print $2}' | /bin/sed 's/[[:space:]]//g' | /bin/head -1)
  if [ -z \"$datadir\" ]; then
  datadir=\"/var/lib/mysql\"
  fi

  if [ -d \"$datadir\" ]; then
  ls_output=$(/bin/ls -ld \"$datadir\" 2>/dev/null)
  if /bin/echo \"$ls_output\" | /bin/grep -q \"^drwxr-x---.*mysql.*mysql\"; then
  /bin/echo \"PASS: $datadir has appropriate permissions (750) and ownership (mysql:mysql)\"
  else
  /bin/echo \"FAIL: $datadir permissions or ownership incorrect\"
  /bin/echo \"Current: $ls_output\"
  fi
  else
  /bin/echo \"FAIL: datadir $datadir does not exist\"
  fi
  }"
      expect      : "^PASS:"
    </custom_item>

    <report type:"WARNING">
      description : "3.10 Secure MySQL Keyring"
      info        : "When configured to use a Keyring plugin or Keyring Component, internal MySQL components and plugins may securely store sensitive information for later retrieval. Associated files for the selected keyring type should have proper permissions.

Limiting the accessibility of these objects will protect the confidentiality, integrity, and availability of internal MySQL component and plugin information.

NOTE: Nessus has not performed this check. Please review the benchmark to ensure target compliance."
      solution    : "MySQL Keyring Remediation Procedures

If no keyring component or plugin is configured, one must be installed and configured. Components are the recommended long-term approach and should be used where possible. Configuration instructions for each component can be found at:

Components:

 - Keyring File - https://dev.mysql.com/doc/refman/9.7/en/keyring-file-component.html
 - Keyring Encrypted File - https://dev.mysql.com/doc/refman/9.7/en/keyring-encrypted-file-component.html
 - Keyring AWS - https://dev.mysql.com/doc/refman/9.7/en/keyring-aws-component.html
 - Keyring HashiCorp Vault - https://dev.mysql.com/doc/refman/9.7/en/keyring-hashicorp-component.html
 - Keyring OCI Vault - https://dev.mysql.com/doc/refman/9.7/en/keyring-oci-component.html
 - Keyring KMIP - https://dev.mysql.com/doc/refman/9.7/en/keyring-kmip-component.html

If a legacy plugin must be used, see the MySQL 9.7 Keyring documentationfor plugin configuration, noting that all plugins are superseded or deprecated and should be migrated to their component equivalents.

To correct file permissions on any keyring file:

chmod 750 <keyring_file>
chown mysql:mysql <keyring_file>"
